md CRASHES. It dies on SIGABRT, which the harness reports as exit -6.

This is the same defect as in format-refuses-a-non-finite-number-in-frontmatter,
reached down a second path. A frontmatter value of .nan reaches
JSONSerialization, which RAISES an Objective-C exception rather than throwing,
so the catch at ListCommand.swift:226 never runs and the process aborts.

It costs more here than in `format`. `md list` walks a directory, so ONE bad
file among hundreds takes down the whole run, and the files already scanned
print nothing. Every other per-file failure in `list` is reported to stderr
and the walk continues; this one should behave the same way.

What it should do: report the file and the key on stderr, skip that file, and
carry on. Exit non-zero at the end, as `list` already does for a file it could
not read.

Read the marker in format-refuses-a-non-finite-number-in-frontmatter for the
cause and the fix.
